{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Voice Cloning & Voice Conversion Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: decompose with recognition-synthesis (code-only demo in main.py)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def clone_pipeline(ref_audio, text, target_embedder, tts_model):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    speaker_emb = target_embedder.encode(ref_audio)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mel = tts_model(text, speaker=speaker_emb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return vocoder(mel)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Conceptually simple; implementation mass is in `tts_model` and speaker encoder."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: zero-shot clone with F5-TTS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from f5_tts.api import F5TTS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tts = F5TTS()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "wav = tts.infer("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ref_file=\"rohit_5s.wav\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ref_text=\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gen_text=\"Please add milk and bread to my list.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Reference transcript must exactly match the audio; mismatch breaks alignment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: voice conversion with KNN-VC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from knnvc import KNNVC  # 2023 model, https://github.com/bshall/knn-vc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vc = KNNVC.load(\"wavlm-base-plus\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "out_wav = vc.convert(source=\"my_voice.wav\", target_pool=[\"alice_1.wav\", \"alice_2.wav\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "KNN-VC runs WavLM to extract per-frame embeddings for source and target pool, then replaces each source frame with its nearest neighbor in the pool. Non-parametric, works with a minute of target speech."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: embed a watermark"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from silentcipher import SilentCipher"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sc = SilentCipher(model=\"2024-06-01\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "payload = b\"consent_id:abc123;ts:1745353200\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "watermarked = sc.embed(wav, sr=24000, message=payload)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "detected = sc.detect(watermarked, sr=24000)   # returns payload bytes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "~32 bits of payload, detectable after MP3 re-encode and light noise."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: consent gate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cloned_inference(text, ref_audio, consent_record):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    assert verify_signature(consent_record), \"Signed consent required\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    assert consent_record[\"speaker_id\"] == hash_speaker(ref_audio)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    wav = tts.infer(ref_file=ref_audio, gen_text=text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    wav = watermark(wav, payload=consent_record[\"id\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return wav"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Demonstrates the speaker-embedding swap by computing the cosine between two \"speakers\" pre and post swap.\n2. **Medium.** Use OpenVoice v2 to clone your own voice. Measure SECS between reference and clone. Measure CER via Whisper.\n3. **Hard.** Apply SilentCipher watermark to 20 clones, run them through 128 kbps MP3 encode+decode, detect the payload. Report bit-accuracy."
      ]
    }
